SOAPBOX: The low bands were poor here with many weak auroral-sounding signals, not good for
SOAPBOX: the scoring bias, and conditions on the high bands were mediocre with the bands
SOAPBOX: closing early, especially to NA. We were definitely not in the right place for this one...
SOAPBOX: It seemed like a lot of people were forced on to 40m for too long, which made it
SOAPBOX: complete bedlam! Congrats to IP2A for a great score and thanks to all our other
SOAPBOX: contesting friends for a fun battle. 73 de EI7M.
